    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d465">

                <pb facs="0553" n="473" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg473"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr.
                            Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-05-27"><hi rendition="#italic">May 27,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 641.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith copy of a letter from
                    Hon. J. N. W. Rumple, a member of Congress from Iowa, in regard to one Francis
                    Connelly, a native of Davenport, Iowa, who is said to be held by the British
                    Government as a prisoner of war on the island of Ceylon.</p>
                <p>You may inquire whether it is possible for this young man to be released on
                    parole on condition that he will return to the United States.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d465-a1.xml" xpointer="d465-a1"/>
            </div>
